title: Razem futures

# The post-2025 Razem fork uses the existing Razem component and the generic
# tak_rozwoj successor slot. The latter can legally represent either Akcja
# Socjalistyczna or Tak! Dla Rozwoju; polling and election code still see one
# additional Left-family committee rather than a bespoke election system.

@matysiak_control_result
# prose-audit: Grade A — The congress result names both statutory chairs, quantifies the internal parliamentary and activist division, and gives every neighbouring Left current a reaction without creating a reaction-event queue.
title: Matysiak wins control of Razem
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
const clampFuture = function(value, low, high) {
    return Math.max(low, Math.min(high, Number(value) || 0));
};
const razemSeats = Math.max(
    0,
    Math.round(Number(Q.razem_party_formed
        ? Q.razem_party_seats
        : Q.razem_seats) || 0)
);
const razemActivists = Math.max(
    1,
    Number(Q.razem_party_formed
        ? Q.razem_exit_strength
        : Q.razem_strength) || 1
);
const matysiakShare = clampFuture(
    0.48 + (Number(Q.matysiak_development_score) || 0) * 0.003 +
        (Number(Q.matysiak_caucus_actions) || 0) * 0.025 +
        (Number(Q.matysiak_development_pressure) || 0) * 0.0015,
    0.54,
    0.78
);
Q.razem_future_route = "matysiak_razem";
Q.razem_future_start_time = Number(Q.time) || 0;
Q.razem_future_outcome = "Matysiak controls Razem without a legal split";
Q.matysiak_project_active = 1;
Q.zandberg_project_active = 0;
Q.matysiak_project_party = "Razem";
Q.zandberg_project_party = "Razem internal minority";
Q.matysiak_developmentalist_strength = Math.round(
    razemActivists * matysiakShare
);
Q.zandberg_socialist_strength = Math.max(
    0,
    Math.round(razemActivists - Q.matysiak_developmentalist_strength)
);
Q.matysiak_project_parliamentary_support = Math.round(
    razemSeats * matysiakShare
);
Q.zandberg_project_parliamentary_support = Math.max(
    0,
    razemSeats - Q.matysiak_project_parliamentary_support
);
Q.razem_future_retained_seats = razemSeats;
Q.razem_future_departing_seats = 0;
Q.razem_leader = "Paulina Matysiak";
Q.razem_co_leader =
    Q.razem_co_leader != "Vacant" &&
    Q.razem_co_leader != "Paulina Matysiak" &&
    !(Q.razem_co_leader == "Magdalena Biejat" && Q.biejat_party != "Razem")
        ? Q.razem_co_leader
        : "Marcelina Zawisza";
Q.razem_leadership_result =
    "Paulina Matysiak and " + Q.razem_co_leader +
    " co-chair a developmentalist Razem";
Q.razem_ideology =
    "State-led development, labour economics and social conservatism";
Q.razem_right_score = 62;
Q.razem_legal_status = "registered political party";
Q.razem_party_name = "Razem";
Q.matysiak_status = "Co-chair of Razem";
Q.matysiak_party = "Razem";
Q.zandberg_party = "Razem";
Q.zandberg_status = "Razem socialist minority organiser";
Q.matysiak_resolution_done = 1;
Q.matysiak_project_ai_state = "Preparing a state-development convention";
Q.left_right_score += 7;
Q.labor_credibility += 4;
Q.union_trust += 2;
Q.progressive_credibility -= 5;
Q.progressives_dissent += 7;
Q.barons_dissent += 3;
Q.pps_dissent += 2;
Q.pis_relation += 2;
Q.ko_relation -= 3;
Q.razem_dissent = Math.max(0, (Number(Q.razem_dissent) || 0) - 4);
Q.razem_cohesion = Math.min(100, (Number(Q.razem_cohesion) || 0) + 5);
Q.razem_cooperation = Math.max(
    0,
    Math.min(100, (Number(Q.razem_cooperation) || 0) - 2)
);
Q.razem_poll_momentum = (Number(Q.razem_poll_momentum) || 0) + 0.7;
Q.news_headline =
    "Matysiak wins Razem's first chair while its second chair remains in office";
!}

= November 2025 — Matysiak wins the first chair

The count gives **Paulina Matysiak** control of Razem's political line, not a
single-leader presidency. **[+ razem_co_leader +]** retains the second chair
under the party's statute. Of the party's current parliamentary support,
**[+ matysiak_project_parliamentary_support +] MPs** backed the developmental
mandate; **[+ zandberg_project_parliamentary_support +]** remain closer to
Zandberg's socialist opposition. The membership division is recorded too:
**[+ matysiak_developmentalist_strength +]** points of organisational strength
follow the new line, while **[+ zandberg_socialist_strength +]** stay in its
internal socialist minority.

Matysiak keeps the labour-economics case and adds rail, nuclear power, regional
investment and economic sovereignty. Wspólne Jutro and the progressive current
fear the cultural retreat; Lewica Pracy and union organisers welcome the
investment argument but ask for bargaining rights. SLD sees a competitor for
regional authority, PPS demands a socialist floor, PiS praises the sovereignty
language and the liberal opposition attacks its cost and conservative allies.

- @poland_event_queue: Record the two-chair result

@split_result
title: Divide Razem's organisation and parliamentary support
on-arrival: {!
const clampFuture = function(value, low, high) {
    return Math.max(low, Math.min(high, Number(value) || 0));
};
const akcja = Q.matysiak_exit_choice == "Akcja Socjalistyczna";
const sourceIsParty = !!Q.razem_party_formed;
const sourceSeats = Math.max(
    0,
    Math.round(Number(sourceIsParty ? Q.razem_party_seats : Q.razem_seats) || 0)
);
const sourceActivists = Math.max(
    1,
    Number(sourceIsParty ? Q.razem_exit_strength : Q.razem_strength) || 1
);
const matysiakEdge = clampFuture(
    ((Number(Q.matysiak_development_score) || 0) - 28) / 54 +
        (Number(Q.matysiak_caucus_actions) || 0) * 0.07 +
        (Number(Q.matysiak_development_pressure) || 0) * 0.002,
    0,
    1
);
const departingShare = akcja
    ? clampFuture(0.52 - matysiakEdge * 0.18, 0.30, 0.52)
    : clampFuture(0.16 + matysiakEdge * 0.30, 0.18, 0.46);
const maximumDeparture = akcja
    ? Math.max(0, sourceSeats - 1)
    : (sourceSeats > 1 ? sourceSeats - 1 : sourceSeats);
const minimumDeparture = sourceSeats > (akcja ? 1 : 0) ? 1 : 0;
const departingSeats = Math.min(
    maximumDeparture,
    Math.max(minimumDeparture, Math.round(sourceSeats * departingShare))
);
const departingActivists = Math.max(
    1,
    Math.round(sourceActivists * departingShare)
);
if (sourceIsParty) {
    Q.razem_party_seats = Math.max(0, sourceSeats - departingSeats);
    Q.razem_exit_strength = Math.max(
        0,
        sourceActivists - departingActivists
    );
} else {
    Q.razem_seats = Math.max(0, sourceSeats - departingSeats);
    Q.left_seats = Math.max(0, (Number(Q.left_seats) || 0) - departingSeats);
    Q.razem_strength = Math.max(0, sourceActivists - departingActivists);
}
Q.tak_rozwoj_seats =
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.tak_rozwoj_seats) || 0) + departingSeats;
Q.razem_future_departing_seats = departingSeats;
Q.razem_future_retained_seats = Math.max(0, sourceSeats - departingSeats);
Q.razem_future_activists = departingActivists;
Q.razem_future_faction_strength = departingActivists;
Q.razem_future_parliamentary_support = departingSeats;
Q.razem_retained_parliamentary_support = Math.max(
    0,
    sourceSeats - departingSeats
);
Q.razem_future_start_time = Number(Q.time) || 0;
Q.matysiak_resolution_done = 1;
Q.tak_dla_rozwoju_party_formed = 1;
Q.razem_successor_party_formed = 1;
Q.tak_rozwoj_legal_status = "registered political party";
Q.tak_rozwoj_list_committee = "tak_rozwoj";
Q.tak_rozwoj_ai_active = 1;
Q.tak_rozwoj_ai_strategy = "Build an independent organisation";
Q.tak_rozwoj_ai_acted = 0;
Q.tak_rozwoj_parent_relation = 28;
Q.tak_rozwoj_poll_momentum =
    (Number(Q.tak_rozwoj_poll_momentum) || 0) +
    (akcja ? 1.2 : 0.8 + matysiakEdge * 0.8);
Q.poll_state_month_key = -1;
Q.razem_dissent = Math.max(0, (Number(Q.razem_dissent) || 0) - 7);
Q.razem_cohesion = Math.max(0, (Number(Q.razem_cohesion) || 0) - 3);
Q.razem_cooperation = Math.max(0, (Number(Q.razem_cooperation) || 0) - 6);
if (akcja) {
    Q.razem_future_route = "akcja_socjalistyczna";
    Q.razem_future_outcome =
        "Matysiak keeps Razem; Zandberg creates Akcja Socjalistyczna";
    Q.akcja_socjalistyczna_party_formed = 1;
    Q.tak_dla_rozwoju_legal_party_formed = 0;
    Q.tak_rozwoj_party_name = "Akcja Socjalistyczna";
    Q.tak_rozwoj_leader = "Adrian Zandberg";
    Q.akcja_socjalistyczna_activists = departingActivists;
    Q.akcja_socjalistyczna_credibility = Math.round(
        (Number(Q.labor_credibility) || 0) * 0.45 +
        (Number(Q.progressive_credibility) || 0) * 0.25 +
        departingActivists
    );
    Q.matysiak_project_active = 1;
    Q.zandberg_project_active = 1;
    Q.matysiak_project_party = "Razem";
    Q.zandberg_project_party = "Akcja Socjalistyczna";
    Q.matysiak_project_ai_state =
        "Preparing Razem's state-development convention";
    Q.zandberg_project_ai_state =
        "Building Akcja Socjalistyczna's socialist organisation";
    Q.matysiak_developmentalist_strength = Math.max(
        0,
        sourceActivists - departingActivists
    );
    Q.zandberg_socialist_strength = departingActivists;
    Q.matysiak_project_parliamentary_support =
        Q.razem_future_retained_seats;
    Q.zandberg_project_parliamentary_support = departingSeats;
    Q.razem_leader = "Paulina Matysiak";
    Q.razem_co_leader =
        Q.razem_co_leader != "Vacant" &&
        Q.razem_co_leader != "Adrian Zandberg" &&
        !(Q.razem_co_leader == "Magdalena Biejat" && Q.biejat_party != "Razem")
            ? Q.razem_co_leader
            : "Marcelina Zawisza";
    Q.razem_leadership_result =
        "Paulina Matysiak and " + Q.razem_co_leader +
        " co-chair Razem after Zandberg founds Akcja Socjalistyczna";
    Q.razem_ideology =
        "State-led development, labour economics and social conservatism";
    Q.razem_right_score = 62;
    Q.matysiak_status = "Co-chair of Razem";
    Q.matysiak_party = "Razem";
    Q.matysiak_has_sejm_mandate = Math.max(
        1,
        Number(Q.matysiak_has_sejm_mandate) || 0
    );
    Q.zandberg_party = "Akcja Socjalistyczna";
    Q.zandberg_status = "Leader of Akcja Socjalistyczna";
    Q.zandberg_advisor = 0;
    Q.advisor_reshuffle_removed_zandberg = 1;
    Q.left_right_score += 7;
    Q.labor_credibility += 3;
    Q.union_trust += 2;
    Q.progressive_credibility -= 3;
    Q.progressives_dissent += 5;
    Q.barons_dissent += 2;
    Q.pps_dissent -= 2;
    Q.pis_relation += 2;
    Q.ko_relation -= 3;
    Q.news_headline =
        "Matysiak keeps Razem while Zandberg registers Akcja Socjalistyczna";
} else {
    Q.razem_future_route = "tak_dla_rozwoju";
    Q.razem_future_outcome =
        "Zandberg keeps Razem; Matysiak creates Tak! Dla Rozwoju";
    Q.akcja_socjalistyczna_party_formed = 0;
    Q.tak_dla_rozwoju_legal_party_formed = 1;
    Q.tak_rozwoj_party_name = "Tak! Dla Rozwoju";
    Q.tak_rozwoj_leader = "Paulina Matysiak";
    Q.tak_rozwoj_activists = departingActivists;
    Q.tak_rozwoj_development_credibility = Math.round(
        (Number(Q.matysiak_development_score) || 0) * 0.55 +
        (Number(Q.labor_credibility) || 0) * 0.25 +
        departingActivists
    );
    Q.matysiak_project_active = 1;
    Q.zandberg_project_active = 1;
    Q.matysiak_project_party = "Tak! Dla Rozwoju";
    Q.zandberg_project_party = "Razem";
    Q.matysiak_project_ai_state =
        "Building Tak! Dla Rozwoju's regional organisation";
    Q.zandberg_project_ai_state =
        "Preparing Razem's democratic-socialist convention";
    Q.matysiak_developmentalist_strength = departingActivists;
    Q.zandberg_socialist_strength = Math.max(
        0,
        sourceActivists - departingActivists
    );
    Q.matysiak_project_parliamentary_support = departingSeats;
    Q.zandberg_project_parliamentary_support =
        Q.razem_future_retained_seats;
    Q.razem_leader = "Adrian Zandberg";
    Q.razem_co_leader =
        Q.razem_co_leader != "Vacant" &&
        Q.razem_co_leader != "Paulina Matysiak" &&
        !(Q.razem_co_leader == "Magdalena Biejat" && Q.biejat_party != "Razem")
            ? Q.razem_co_leader
            : "Marcelina Zawisza";
    Q.razem_leadership_result =
        "Adrian Zandberg and " + Q.razem_co_leader +
        " co-chair Razem after Matysiak founds Tak! Dla Rozwoju";
    Q.razem_ideology =
        "Democratic socialism, public ownership and movement organisation";
    Q.razem_right_score = Math.min(30, Number(Q.razem_right_score) || 18);
    Q.matysiak_advisor = 0;
    Q.matysiak_has_sejm_mandate = departingSeats > 0 ? 1 : 0;
    Q.matysiak_status = "Leader of Tak! Dla Rozwoju";
    Q.matysiak_party = "tak_rozwoj";
    Q.zandberg_party = "Razem";
    Q.zandberg_status = "Co-chair of Razem";
    Q.matysiak_development_pressure += 8;
    Q.labor_credibility += 2;
    Q.union_trust += 1;
    Q.progressive_credibility += 2;
    Q.progressives_dissent -= 2;
    Q.barons_dissent += 3;
    Q.pps_dissent += 1;
    Q.pis_relation += 3;
    Q.ko_relation -= 2;
    Q.news_headline =
        "Zandberg keeps Razem while Matysiak registers Tak! Dla Rozwoju";
}
!}
go-to: akcja_foundation_result if matysiak_exit_choice = "Akcja Socjalistyczna"; tak_foundation_result if matysiak_exit_choice = "Tak! Dla Rozwoju"

@akcja_foundation_result
# prose-audit: Grade A — Zandberg is correctly the departing leader, Akcja receives a legal identity and proportional organisation, and the surrounding Left and opposition actors react from their own interests.
title: Zandberg leaves Razem and creates Akcja Socjalistyczna
new-page: true

= November 2025 — Two socialist claims, two legal parties

**Paulina Matysiak** and **[+ razem_co_leader +]** retain Razem's two chairs.
**Adrian Zandberg** registers **Akcja Socjalistyczna** as a separate political
party. **[+ razem_future_departing_seats +] MPs** and **[+
akcja_socjalistyczna_activists +] points** of organisational strength follow
him; **[+ razem_future_retained_seats +] MPs** and **[+
matysiak_developmentalist_strength +] points** remain with developmentalist
Razem. The generic successor-party polling and election ledger will count
Akcja under its own legal name and five-percent threshold.

Akcja takes the housing organisers, public-ownership campaigners and much of
the movement socialist network. Matysiak keeps more of the regional investment
operation. Wspólne Jutro and the progressives will cooperate with Akcja on
rights but distrust another male-led rival; Lewica Pracy, PPS and unions welcome
its labour programme while refusing automatic allegiance. SLD welcomes a
divided challenger. PiS courts Matysiak on sovereignty and attacks Akcja's
ownership plans; KO warns that two Left committees can both miss the threshold.

Akcja's advantage is a credible movement and labour organisation. Its cost is
electoral isolation and weaker access to the wider Left's lists.

- @poland_event_queue: Put both membership rolls on the desk

@tak_foundation_result
# prose-audit: Grade A — Matysiak's departure creates a legally and organisationally distinct developmental party, while Razem's two-chair leadership and socialist remainder stay explicit.
title: Matysiak leaves Razem and creates Tak! Dla Rozwoju
new-page: true

= November 2025 — Development becomes a legal party

**Adrian Zandberg** and **[+ razem_co_leader +]** retain Razem's two chairs.
**Paulina Matysiak** registers **Tak! Dla Rozwoju** as a separate political
party. Her network takes **[+ razem_future_departing_seats +] MPs** and **[+
tak_rozwoj_activists +] points** of organisational strength; socialist Razem
keeps **[+ razem_future_retained_seats +] MPs** and **[+
zandberg_socialist_strength +] points**. Prior development organising, caucus
work and the congress score determined the division.

Tak! begins with rail, nuclear power, public investment, regional development
and economic sovereignty. Wspólne Jutro and the progressive current oppose its
social-conservative edge; Lewica Pracy and unions insist that state investment
must create bargaining power, while PPS demands public ownership rather than
subsidies. SLD sees a regional rival. PiS offers votes for selected projects
and KO's liberals attack the expense and cross-party ambiguity.

Tak!'s advantage is ownership of state capacity and regional investment. Its
cost is progressive distrust and a permanently uncertain relationship with the
broader Left.

- @poland_event_queue: Register the developmental party

@zandberg_strategy
# prose-audit: Grade A — Housing, ownership, labour and green industry are staged as an argument between movement durability and list survival, with an authored advantage and cost on both choices.
title: Zandberg decides whether a socialist movement can survive an election
subtitle: Housing, public ownership, labour power and green industry compete with the need for a viable list.
new-page: true
tags: poland_event
priority: 27
order: 8
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and zandberg_project_active = 1 and zandberg_future_decision_done = 0 and time >= razem_future_start_time + 3 and year <= 2027

= [+ date_label +] — A movement with a ballot deadline

**Adrian Zandberg** has built a programme around municipal housing, public
ownership, stronger unions and a green industrial transition. In **[+
zandberg_project_party +]**, organisers now disagree about sequence. Movement
councils can make the party durable and distinct, but an independent committee
can waste that strength below five percent. A common-list compact protects the
mandates and asks activists to trust the organisations they left or criticised.

- @zandberg_movement
- @zandberg_electoral

@zandberg_movement
title: Build housing and workplace councils before bargaining over lists
subtitle: Advantage: movement organisation and labour credibility. Cost: a separate five-percent campaign remains possible.
on-arrival: {!
Q.zandberg_future_decision_done = 1;
Q.zandberg_future_strategy = "Movement socialist councils";
Q.zandberg_housing_program += 6;
Q.zandberg_public_ownership_program += 6;
Q.zandberg_green_industry_program += 5;
Q.movement_autonomy += 6;
Q.organiser_energy += 4;
Q.labor_credibility += 5;
Q.union_trust += 4;
Q.workers_support += 3;
Q.public_sector_support += 2;
Q.ko_relation -= 4;
Q.barons_dissent += 3;
Q.progressives_dissent -= 1;
if (Q.zandberg_project_party == "Akcja Socjalistyczna") {
    Q.tak_rozwoj_list_committee = "tak_rozwoj";
    Q.tak_rozwoj_parent_relation -= 5;
    Q.tak_rozwoj_organisation =
        (Number(Q.tak_rozwoj_organisation) || 20) + 8;
    Q.tak_rozwoj_poll_momentum += 0.8;
    Q.tak_rozwoj_ai_strategy = "Build a movement before list bargaining";
} else {
    Q.razem_list_committee = Q.razem_party_formed ? "razem" : "left";
    Q.razem_party_relation -= Q.razem_party_formed ? 4 : 0;
    Q.razem_poll_momentum = (Number(Q.razem_poll_momentum) || 0) + 0.8;
}
Q.zandberg_project_ai_state = "Housing and workplace council campaign";
Q.news_headline =
    "Zandberg puts housing and workplace councils before list arithmetic";
!}

The councils recruit tenants, shop stewards and public-service workers around
projects they can audit. Akcja or Razem gains a social base that survives a bad
poll. SLD and KO immediately print the five-percent line; unions answer that a
party without organised workers can survive a ballot and still disappear.

- @poland_event_queue: Open the socialist councils

@zandberg_electoral
title: Negotiate a common-list compact around housing and green industry
subtitle: Advantage: electoral survival and wider reach. Cost: movement autonomy and a sharper public-ownership line are traded for list guarantees.
on-arrival: {!
Q.zandberg_future_decision_done = 1;
Q.zandberg_future_strategy = "Socialist electoral compact";
Q.zandberg_housing_program += 5;
Q.zandberg_public_ownership_program += 2;
Q.zandberg_green_industry_program += 6;
Q.movement_autonomy -= 5;
Q.organiser_energy -= 2;
Q.labor_credibility += 2;
Q.union_trust -= 2;
Q.ko_relation += 2;
Q.razem_cooperation += 5;
Q.party_unity += 3;
Q.barons_dissent += 2;
Q.pps_dissent += 2;
if (Q.zandberg_project_party == "Akcja Socjalistyczna") {
    Q.tak_rozwoj_list_committee = "left";
    Q.tak_rozwoj_parent_relation += 18;
    Q.tak_rozwoj_poll_momentum += 0.3;
    Q.tak_rozwoj_ai_strategy = "Seek protected places on the common Left list";
} else if (Q.razem_party_formed) {
    Q.razem_list_committee = "left_coalition";
    Q.razem_party_relation += 12;
    Q.razem_poll_momentum = (Number(Q.razem_poll_momentum) || 0) + 0.3;
} else {
    Q.left_poll_momentum = (Number(Q.left_poll_momentum) || 0) + 0.4;
}
Q.zandberg_project_ai_state = "Common-list socialist compact";
Q.news_headline =
    "Zandberg trades list guarantees for a common housing and industry plank";
!}

The broader Left accepts housing construction, sectoral bargaining and a green
industrial bank as the protected plank. It does not accept a veto over every
future coalition budget. The project is harder to erase at the election and
less able to claim that electoral survival changed nothing.

- @poland_event_queue: Sign the socialist list compact

@matysiak_strategy
# prose-audit: Grade A — Rails, nuclear power and regional investment become a choice between a union-backed Left compact and a sovereignty campaign whose progressive cost is explicit.
title: Matysiak decides what a developmentalist Left is for
subtitle: A labour-development compact competes with a sovereign infrastructure bloc.
